          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            In
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+field+theory"} quantum field theory
            with chiral
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fermions"} fermions
            (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spinor+fields"}> spinor fields
            )
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ψ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \psi
            with
            %em
              chiral version of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dirac+current"} Dirac current
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi J
                    %mo =
                    %mi i
                    %mover
                      %mi Ψ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ¯
                    %mi Γ
                    %mi Ψ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} J = i \bar \Psi \Gamma \Psi
            %em chiral anomaly
            is a non-
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/conserved+current"} conservation
            of this current
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi div
                  %mi J
                  %mo =
                  %mi Anomaly
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  div J = Anomaly
                  \\,.
          %p
            (See at
            = succeed ".)" do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ward+identity"} Ward identity
          %p
            In the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/standard+model+of+particle+physics"} standard model of particle physics
            this happens and plays a role for
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pion"} pion
            decay and for
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/baryogenesis"} baryogenesis
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/baryon+current"} baryon current
            and the anomaly term is the Pontryagin 4-form
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Anomaly
                  %mo =
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟨
                  %msub
                    %mi F
                    %mo ∇
                  %mo ∧
                  %msub
                    %mi F
                    %mo ∇
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟩
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Anomaly = \langle F_\nabla \wedge F_\nabla\rangle
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gauge+field"} gauge field
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo ∇
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \nabla
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/curvature"} curvature
            4-form of the corresponding
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chern-Simons+line+3-bundle"} Chern-Simons line 3-bundle
          %p
            If there are
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/instantons"} instantons
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gauge+field"} gauge field
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/principal+connection"} principal connection
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo ∇
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \nabla
            has a nontrivial underlying
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/principal+bundle"} principal bundle
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chern-Simons+line+3-bundle"} Chern-Simons line 3-bundle
            is topologically nontrivial the anomaly term
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟨
                  %msub
                    %mi F
                    %mo ∇
                  %mo ∧
                  %msub
                    %mi F
                    %mo ∇
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟩
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \langle F_\nabla \wedge F_\nabla\rangle
            is a non-exact integral form, hence the above equation is to be read as the
            %em local
            expression identifying
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo ⋆
                  %mi j
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \star j
            with the local
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/3-connection"} 3-connection
            on the CS 3-bundle.
